<%# The switch's face on the hub (doc/ki_zugang_umbau_plan.md D1/D2, reshaped by
    doc/ki_uebersicht_zeilenliste_plan.md D1, D4, D6).

    One sentence, no box, no icon. The green box it replaces read as "all is well" on a
    page where, two lines further down, the access was missing — both were true, the
    box only told one of them. The sentence now carries the second fact itself: it says
    nothing works only when the gate every AI button in the app asks (ai_available?)
    says so, which includes the operator's credential. Whether an access has been
    CHOSEN is the row's business, one line further down.

    No date and no name any more (D4): the Protokoll row says since when the trail
    exists, and the page behind it names every switch with time and person. That is
    where an audit statement belongs.

    Two faces, still unequal (D2 of the Zugang plan): switched off, the consent copy
    stands here in full, because this is where the decision is made and the text
    belongs at the decision. Switched on, one sentence, the link, the way out.

    The switch action is a TEXT action, not a second button: the page has one main
    action in the title row (show.html.erb decides which), and a second filled surface
    would compete with it. Where switching on IS the main action (access chosen, AI
    off) this file renders no action at all. The POST endpoints stay on
    AiSettingsController on purpose (D1 of the Zugang plan): both write with
    update_columns outside any transaction so the compliance off-switch can never be
    blocked. Only their form moved. %>
<% ai_on = @organisation.ai_enabled? %>
<% text_action = 'rounded-sm underline-offset-2 hover:underline focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-black focus-visible:ring-offset-2' %>
<div id="ai_activation" class="mb-8 width-text text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
  <p>
    <% if !ai_on %>
      <%= t('views.organisations.ai_overview.status.inactive') %>
    <% elsif @ai_available %>
      <%= t('views.organisations.ai_overview.status.active') %>
    <% else %>
      <%= t('views.organisations.ai_overview.status.active_without_access') %>
    <% end %>
  </p>
  <% if ai_on %>
    <%# A div, not a p: the switch action is a form, and a <p> cannot hold one — the
        browser would close the paragraph and drop the form onto its own line. %>
    <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2">
      <% privacy_link = legal_page_link(
           :privacy,
           label: t('views.organisations.ai_overview.status.privacy_link'),
           target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener', class: "text-green-700 #{text_action}"
         ) %>
      <% if privacy_link.present? %>
        <%= privacy_link %>
        <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      <% end %>
      <%= button_to t('views.organisations.ai_overview.actions.switch_off'),
                    deactivate_organisation_ai_settings_path(@organisation),
                    method: :post, form_class: 'inline',
                    form: { data: { turbo_confirm: t('views.confirm.ai_deactivate') } },
                    class: "text-body #{text_action}" %>
    </div>
  <% else %>
    <%# The consent copy carries its own privacy link; no second one beneath it. %>
    <%= render 'organisations/shared/opt_in_explanation',
               text_class: 'text-muted',
               link_class: 'hover:text-heading dark:hover:text-cream-100' %>
    <% unless @access_chosen %>
      <%# Nothing chosen yet: "Zugang einrichten" holds the title row, and switching
          on stays reachable as text — the order is a recommendation, not a gate. %>
      <div class="mt-2">
        <%= button_to t('views.organisations.ai_overview.actions.switch_on'),
                      activate_organisation_ai_settings_path(@organisation),
                      method: :post, form_class: 'inline',
                      form: { data: { turbo_confirm: t('views.confirm.ai_activate') } },
                      class: "text-body #{text_action}" %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>
